{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","id":"2cad50c6-c69b-44d9-8bc5-9680ad00c144","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:53:55.620Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"b9dd0bd5a33788d9ca22f5c1531fc92f918cd9ae3201ce2c9539abcac6880adc","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"67ef7045-8044-4130-b487-9254099769b4","keep":137,"tail":["e337c5c4f49ce693860bd8ad78dc17bd2da8da5b11b7546278c9167821b2f55e","415cc387dc22277227e08ea68d339fbc71a939cbb123117664b553c287888a19","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",139,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"5e9f8b4dfe9891320c28addf134446aa6bf976c6043bd289d2b5e250226559c6"}
{"parentUuid":"631347e9-a83d-4f6f-86dd-6d5ab46c974b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn2KZFMgiR3ntvns8UVj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now updating the spec doc to match, then posting the boards here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":279419,"output_tokens":2881,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2881,"cache_read_input_tokens":279419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1128},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn2KYvGm1YRGrNpMxiC7","requestRef":"2cad50c6-c69b-44d9-8bc5-9680ad00c144","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bce31a50-efc3-4561-b252-29a65f7e1570","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:53:56.539Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"bce31a50-efc3-4561-b252-29a65f7e1570","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn2KZFMgiR3ntvns8UVj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B6HKKg4JUnydodixVhcjwX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","content":"# Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)\n\nBoards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.\n\n## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06\n\n- The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser.\n- The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".\n- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\n\nEverything below that is not in this list is a proposal.\n\n## The rule (proposal)\n\nThe app draws credits. The server draws anything about money, inside a sheet the app owns. Where the app shows a price, it shows a sentence the server wrote and never works out a price itself.\n\n## Who draws what (proposal)\n\nApp (ships with each release):\n- **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it.\n- **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link.\n- **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.\n- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.\n- **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\".\n\nServer (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:\n- **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out.\n- **Chargebee checkout**, as today.\n- **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.\n- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\n\n## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)\n\n1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".\n2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that.\n3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.\n4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.\n\n## Constraints found\n\n- **Google sign-in can't run inside a web view.** Google blocks OAuth in embedded web views on purpose. So the signed-out sheet's buttons read \"Sign up to buy\": they close the sheet and put the person on the app's own sign-up card. Source: https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html\n- **Chargebee supports its hosted checkout inside an app's web view.** It ships a React Native wrapper for exactly that. Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases applies to iOS and Android apps, not to a desktop app downloaded from our own site. Source: https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html\n- **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building.\n- **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that.\n\n## Open\n\n- The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.\n- The proration line on Change plan is a placeholder for Chargebee's setting.\n- Boards 5a and 5b (the old pricing page) and 4b's \"Pay as you go\" are superseded. A note on the canvas says so; their builder is unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":279419,"output_tokens":2881,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1128,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2881,"cache_read_input_tokens":279419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1128,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1128},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B6HKKg4JUnydodixVhcjwX":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","content":"# Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)\n\nBoards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.\n\n## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06\n\n- The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser.\n- The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".\n- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\n\nEverything below that is not in this list is a proposal.\n\n## The rule (proposal)\n\nThe app draws credits. The server draws anything about money, inside a sheet the app owns. Where the app shows a price, it shows a sentence the server wrote and never works out a price itself.\n\n## Who draws what (proposal)\n\nApp (ships with each release):\n- **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it.\n- **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link.\n- **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.\n- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.\n- **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\".\n\nServer (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:\n- **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out.\n- **Chargebee checkout**, as today.\n- **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.\n- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\n\n## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)\n\n1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".\n2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that.\n3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.\n4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.\n\n## Constraints found\n\n- **Google sign-in can't run inside a web view.** Google blocks OAuth in embedded web views on purpose. So the signed-out sheet's buttons read \"Sign up to buy\": they close the sheet and put the person on the app's own sign-up card. Source: https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html\n- **Chargebee supports its hosted checkout inside an app's web view.** It ships a React Native wrapper for exactly that. Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases applies to iOS and Android apps, not to a desktop app downloaded from our own site. Source: https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html\n- **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building.\n- **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that.\n\n## Open\n\n- The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.\n- The proration line on Change plan is a placeholder for Chargebee's setting.\n- Boards 5a and 5b (the old pricing page) and 4b's \"Pay as you go\" are superseded. A note on the canvas says so; their builder is unchanged.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgn2KYvGm1YRGrNpMxiC7","requestRef":"2cad50c6-c69b-44d9-8bc5-9680ad00c144","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"618f36a0-ad4a-40e4-aaf6-2de80033c211","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:54:10.383Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"618f36a0-ad4a-40e4-aaf6-2de80033c211","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5a654659-7a68-4526-a481-c199ca4d1cdb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6HKKg4JUnydodixVhcjwX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"bb5cd3e0-15ab-4afc-9843-86c3320395c2","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:54:10.439Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","content":"# Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)\n\nBoards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.\n\n## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06\n\n- The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser.\n- The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".\n- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\n\nEverything below that is not in this list is a proposal.\n\n## The rule (proposal)\n\nThe app draws credits. The server draws anything about money, inside a sheet the app owns. Where the app shows a price, it shows a sentence the server wrote and never works out a price itself.\n\n## Who draws what (proposal)\n\nApp (ships with each release):\n- **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it.\n- **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link.\n- **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.\n- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.\n- **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\".\n\nServer (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:\n- **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out.\n- **Chargebee checkout**, as today.\n- **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.\n- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\n\n## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)\n\n1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".\n2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that.\n3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.\n4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.\n\n## Constraints found\n\n- **Google sign-in can't run inside a web view.** Google blocks OAuth in embedded web views on purpose. So the signed-out sheet's buttons read \"Sign up to buy\": they close the sheet and put the person on the app's own sign-up card. Source: https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html\n- **Chargebee supports its hosted checkout inside an app's web view.** It ships a React Native wrapper for exactly that. Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases applies to iOS and Android apps, not to a desktop app downloaded from our own site. Source: https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html\n- **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building.\n- **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that.\n\n## Open\n\n- The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.\n- The proration line on Change plan is a placeholder for Chargebee's setting.\n- Boards 5a and 5b (the old pricing page) and 4b's \"Pay as you go\" are superseded. A note on the canvas says so; their builder is unchanged.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":55,"newStart":1,"newLines":51,"lines":["-# Money pages: which the app draws, which the server draws (proposal, 2026-11-06)","+# Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)"," ","-Nothing here is agreed. Kenneth asked to put the pricing and plan pages into the first-run design, have the server render the cloud pages where it can, and keep a clear boundary so old app versions keep working.","+Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py."," ","-Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 118). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.","+## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06"," ","-## The rule","+- The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser.","+- The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".","+- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000."," ","-The app shows credits; the server sells them. Anything with a dollar amount, a payment form or a plan change is a server page opened in the browser. The app never shows a dollar amount.","+Everything below that is not in this list is a proposal."," ","-## Who draws what","+## The rule (proposal)"," ","-App (ships with each release):","-- Welcome and Home's agent card: the 500-credit offer, its scale line, a \"See prices ↗\" link.","-- Composer: ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.","-- Preferences › Account: signed-in line, plan name and renewal date (no price), a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (needs local chat titles), savings-alert switch, \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing ↗\".","-- Print history: the report button and \"25 credits added\".","+The app draws credits. The server draws anything about money, inside a sheet the app owns. Where the app shows a price, it shows a sentence the server wrote and never works out a price itself."," ","-Server (jusprinv2.obico.io):","-- Credits and plans (pricing), signed in or out.","-- Chargebee checkout, as today.","-- Thank-you page (new; replaces today's redirect to the v1 chat at /jusprin/v1.0/embedded_chat/).","-- Billing (new): plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.","-- The savings alert's sentence and sums.","+## Who draws what (proposal)"," ","-## The contract between them (the only part old app versions depend on)","+App (ships with each release):","+- **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it.","+- **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link.","+- **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.","+- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.","+- **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\"."," ","-1. GET /v2/account, as today. Fields are only added, never renamed or removed; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. The app reads it again whenever its window becomes active, which is how \"+1,000 credits\" appears after paying.","-2. New: POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from: \"welcome\" | \"composer_low\" | \"out_of_credits\" | \"preferences\" | \"alert\"} → {url}. When signed in, the URL carries a one-time sign-in token (single use, about 60 s) so the browser opens as the app's account, whichever way the person signed in. Signed out, the URL has no token. The server answers these page names forever; an unknown name opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the URL itself (AgentConfiguration.cpp cloud_pricing_url, gateway + \"/ent/jusprin/pricing/\"), so this replaces that.","-3. The account answer's unused `suggestion` slot (web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py) carries {text, page}. The app shows the text as written and opens the page through a page link.","+Server (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:","+- **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out.","+- **Chargebee checkout**, as today.","+- **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.","+- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.","+- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert."," ","-## Confusing spots this fixes","+## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)"," ","-- After signing in with email in the app, the browser is probably signed out (unverified), so a person could buy on a different account. Fixed by the page link.","-- \"Pay as you go\" shown as the plan of someone who never paid. Now \"No plan\".","-- The pricing card said \"500 credits\" while its launch note said \"$10 buys 1,000\". The card now says 1,000 with \"double the usual 500\" under it.","-- The pricing page showed neither balance nor current plan. Now a line at the top says both, and the current plan's button reads \"Your plan\".","-- Nothing after paying said to go back to the app. The thank-you page does.","-- The app's Account and a server account page would share a name. The server page is \"Billing\".","-- Nothing defined where Manage plan went. It becomes \"Billing ↗\".","-- An expired link lands on the signed-out pricing page with a line saying why, not an error.","+1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".","+2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that.","+3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.","+4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written."," ","-## Server work this needs","+## Constraints found"," ","-- web_link endpoint and token sign-in (new).","-- Pricing page v2 (the v1 page at /ent/jusprin/pricing/ offers Free and Unlimited $6.99).","-- Thank-you and Billing pages.","-- Moving the savings-alert arithmetic from the app into `suggestion`.","+- **Google sign-in can't run inside a web view.** Google blocks OAuth in embedded web views on purpose. So the signed-out sheet's buttons read \"Sign up to buy\": they close the sheet and put the person on the app's own sign-up card. Source: https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html","+- **Chargebee supports its hosted checkout inside an app's web view.** It ships a React Native wrapper for exactly that. Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases applies to iOS and Android apps, not to a desktop app downloaded from our own site. Source: https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html","+- **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building.","+- **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that."," ","-## App work this needs","+## Open"," ","-- Call web_link instead of building the pricing URL.","-- Refresh the account answer on window activation.","-- Preferences › Account: \"No plan\", drop \"$16 a month\" and the discount line, \"Billing ↗\".","-- Show `suggestion` when present.","+- The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.","+- The proration line on Change plan is a placeholder for Chargebee's setting.","+- Boards 5a and 5b (the old pricing page) and 4b's \"Pay as you go\" are superseded. A note on the canvas says so; their builder is unchanged."]}],"originalFile":"# Money pages: which the app draws, which the server draws (proposal, 2026-11-06)\n\nNothing here is agreed. Kenneth asked to put the pricing and plan pages into the first-run design, have the server render the cloud pages where it can, and keep a clear boundary so old app versions keep working.\n\nBoards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 118). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.\n\n## The rule\n\nThe app shows credits; the server sells them. Anything with a dollar amount, a payment form or a plan change is a server page opened in the browser. The app never shows a dollar amount.\n\n## Who draws what\n\nApp (ships with each release):\n- Welcome and Home's agent card: the 500-credit offer, its scale line, a \"See prices ↗\" link.\n- Composer: ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.\n- Preferences › Account: signed-in line, plan name and renewal date (no price), a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (needs local chat titles), savings-alert switch, \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing ↗\".\n- Print history: the report button and \"25 credits added\".\n\nServer (jusprinv2.obico.io):\n- Credits and plans (pricing), signed in or out.\n- Chargebee checkout, as today.\n- Thank-you page (new; replaces today's redirect to the v1 chat at /jusprin/v1.0/embedded_chat/).\n- Billing (new): plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- The savings alert's sentence and sums.\n\n## The contract between them (the only part old app versions depend on)\n\n1. GET /v2/account, as today. Fields are only added, never renamed or removed; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. The app reads it again whenever its window becomes active, which is how \"+1,000 credits\" appears after paying.\n2. New: POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from: \"welcome\" | \"composer_low\" | \"out_of_credits\" | \"preferences\" | \"alert\"} → {url}. When signed in, the URL carries a one-time sign-in token (single use, about 60 s) so the browser opens as the app's account, whichever way the person signed in. Signed out, the URL has no token. The server answers these page names forever; an unknown name opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the URL itself (AgentConfiguration.cpp cloud_pricing_url, gateway + \"/ent/jusprin/pricing/\"), so this replaces that.\n3. The account answer's unused `suggestion` slot (web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py) carries {text, page}. The app shows the text as written and opens the page through a page link.\n\n## Confusing spots this fixes\n\n- After signing in with email in the app, the browser is probably signed out (unverified), so a person could buy on a different account. Fixed by the page link.\n- \"Pay as you go\" shown as the plan of someone who never paid. Now \"No plan\".\n- The pricing card said \"500 credits\" while its launch note said \"$10 buys 1,000\". The card now says 1,000 with \"double the usual 500\" under it.\n- The pricing page showed neither balance nor current plan. Now a line at the top says both, and the current plan's button reads \"Your plan\".\n- Nothing after paying said to go back to the app. The thank-you page does.\n- The app's Account and a server account page would share a name. The server page is \"Billing\".\n- Nothing defined where Manage plan went. It becomes \"Billing ↗\".\n- An expired link lands on the signed-out pricing page with a line saying why, not an error.\n\n## Server work this needs\n\n- web_link endpoint and token sign-in (new).\n- Pricing page v2 (the v1 page at /ent/jusprin/pricing/ offers Free and Unlimited $6.99).\n- Thank-you and Billing pages.\n- Moving the savings-alert arithmetic from the app into `suggestion`.\n\n## App work this needs\n\n- Call web_link instead of building the pricing URL.\n- Refresh the account answer on window activation.\n- Preferences › Account: \"No plan\", drop \"$16 a month\" and the discount line, \"Billing ↗\".\n- Show `suggestion` when present.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"618f36a0-ad4a-40e4-aaf6-2de80033c211","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
