{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","id":"5f7a8a68-43d4-42e2-88c3-fd3c7ab6a7f7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:54:20.897Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"b9dd0bd5a33788d9ca22f5c1531fc92f918cd9ae3201ce2c9539abcac6880adc","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"cdaebc55-6db9-4d26-a5e9-e448e1e5dab5","keep":143,"tail":["de25520abb519a607e05f5e8c28bf86091c028d34b8d646e643739aa2b7bfc07","aaeab325420034848d8f241e4698a80d44b48d175b987d4a5732800f591e216f","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",145,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"81c26a2e297ff7ea69796a70a6b88604069363140c88325d6ad13f36c328f965"}
{"parentUuid":"38695971-d143-4b17-8945-7c067fdcc5c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn2MRPeDXjvAbQFcxTEk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I redrew the money boards with your three decisions and published them to the canvas (version 121, the \"Credits & plans\" page, from y=2900). Images of all ten are posted above. Your decisions are applied everywhere:\n- **In-app sheet:** the server's pages open in a sheet inside the app instead of the browser.\n- **Credit pack:** the one-time purchase now has that name.\n- **Launch offer:** every credit amount is doubled until 31 Jan.\n\n**How the sheet works.** The app draws only the frame: a title, \"Open in browser\", the close button, and its own loading and can't-load screens (last image). Everything inside the frame is the server's page. Because the app owns the frame, a person never leaves the app. When checkout finishes, the server's page sends the sheet to a fixed \"done\" address. The app then closes the sheet, reads the balance again, and turns Send back on with the typed message still in the box.\n\n**What a person sees, in order:**\n1. The welcome card says \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", how long they last, and what comes after, with a \"See prices\" link.\n2. Before signing up, the sheet shows prices with \"Sign up to buy\" buttons. They send the person back to the app's own sign-up card, because Google sign-in can't run inside the sheet.\n3. From the out-of-credits card, \"Get more credits\" opens the sheet already signed in. The line at the top says the balance and which account gets the credits.\n4. After checkout, the sheet says \"1,000 credits added\" with a \"Back to your chat\" button.\n5. In Preferences › Account, someone without a plan reads \"No plan\", and bought credits appear as \"Credit packs\". \"Billing\" opens the server's Billing page in the sheet, with plan, payment method, invoices and delete account.\n\n**Launch offer on the cards.** Each card shows its doubled amount as the headline: the Credit pack 1,000, Hobby 1,500 a month, Workshop 2,000 a month. A note under each says \"double the usual …\". One rule is my reading, not your words: a plan month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.\n\n**Where the old pricing board sits.** It is still on the canvas, with a note beside it saying these boards replace it. The spec is at [money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md](money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md).\n\n**Decision needed: should Account show the plan's price?** It's yours because it decides whether dollars appear anywhere in the app outside the sheet. In my proposal, the Workshop line in Account reads \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\". The server writes that sentence, and the app only displays it, so a price change still needs no release. It costs one extra field in the account data that the server must keep sending in later versions. The alternative is no dollars in Account at all: the person opens Billing to see what they pay, and the server owes the app nothing extra. I'd keep the server-written line, because Account is where people look for what they pay."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":283643,"output_tokens":966,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":283643,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":396},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn2MQy69AmRZF7rWyb58","requestRef":"5f7a8a68-43d4-42e2-88c3-fd3c7ab6a7f7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"784e3395-5360-4509-9879-b3f202bf31a3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:54:30.263Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
