{"parentUuid":"c2ac4a26-91e2-44fd-92f7-b66456c0d1ac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn3A3a2mF7atXGyb4Ymn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017F1HTeKG3xPHL5N8yeWC8L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"(version 121)\",\"(version 123)\")\nrep(\"\"\"- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000. It should look celebratory: the boards show a gradient banner, \"Double credits on everything\", and a \"2× launch bonus\" badge with the usual amount struck through on every card.\n- Account shows the plan's price as a line the server sends; no price is hardcoded in the app.\n- Delete account lives at the end of Preferences › Account, not on the server's page.\n- Usage per day and per chat lives on the server's page, now \"Billing and usage\", not in the app.\"\"\")\nrep(\"plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \\\"Get more credits\\\" and \\\"Billing\\\" open the sheet.\",\n    \"plan name with the server-sent price line, a bar per kind of credit, the savings-alert switch, and Delete account (the app's own confirmation dialog, whose sentence the server sends; then DELETE /v2/account and sign out). \\\"Get more credits\\\", the ring's \\\"See usage\\\" and \\\"Billing and usage\\\" open the sheet.\")\nrep(\"- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\",\n    \"- **Billing and usage:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, credits left, and credits used per day and per chat. The server doesn't know chat titles today (`account.py` names a row by its chat id). Titles are generated through the gateway (request kind `title`), so it can keep the title it returns.\")\nrep(\"- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\", \"- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line, the delete warning and the savings alert.\")\nrep(\"One new field: the plan's price line,\", \"New fields: the plan's price line and the delete warning, each a finished sentence; the price line reads\")\nrep(\"4. **The `suggestion` slot**\", \"4. **DELETE /v2/account** deletes the account; the app then signs out.\\n5. **The `suggestion` slot**\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md <<'EOF'\nSame day, version 123 (1793984692-0fde), Kenneth: celebratory launch offer (gradient banner + \"2× launch bonus\" badges, struck-through usual amounts), price line sent by the server, Delete account moved to Preferences › Account (new money-10 with the confirmation dialog), usage moved to the server page now titled \"Billing and usage\".\nEOF\necho ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2945,"cache_read_input_tokens":320405,"output_tokens":2118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":40},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2945,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2118,"cache_read_input_tokens":320405,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2945},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017F1HTeKG3xPHL5N8yeWC8L":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]; s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"(version 121)\",\"(version 123)\")\nrep(\"\"\"- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000. It should look celebratory: the boards show a gradient banner, \"Double credits on everything\", and a \"2× launch bonus\" badge with the usual amount struck through on every card.\n- Account shows the plan's price as a line the server sends; no price is hardcoded in the app.\n- Delete account lives at the end of Preferences › Account, not on the server's page.\n- Usage per day and per chat lives on the server's page, now \"Billing and usage\", not in the app.\"\"\")\nrep(\"plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \\\"Get more credits\\\" and \\\"Billing\\\" open the sheet.\",\n    \"plan name with the server-sent price line, a bar per kind of credit, the savings-alert switch, and Delete account (the app's own confirmation dialog, whose sentence the server sends; then DELETE /v2/account and sign out). \\\"Get more credits\\\", the ring's \\\"See usage\\\" and \\\"Billing and usage\\\" open the sheet.\")\nrep(\"- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\",\n    \"- **Billing and usage:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, credits left, and credits used per day and per chat. The server doesn't know chat titles today (`account.py` names a row by its chat id). Titles are generated through the gateway (request kind `title`), so it can keep the title it returns.\")\nrep(\"- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\", \"- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line, the delete warning and the savings alert.\")\nrep(\"One new field: the plan's price line,\", \"New fields: the plan's price line and the delete warning, each a finished sentence; the price line reads\")\nrep(\"4. **The `suggestion` slot**\", \"4. **DELETE /v2/account** deletes the account; the app then signs out.\\n5. **The `suggestion` slot**\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md <<'EOF'\nSame day, version 123 (1793984692-0fde), Kenneth: celebratory launch offer (gradient banner + \"2× launch bonus\" badges, struck-through usual amounts), price line sent by the server, Delete account moved to Preferences › Account (new money-10 with the confirmation dialog), usage moved to the server page now titled \"Billing and usage\".\nEOF\necho ok"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgn3A3JAckVPMioXsvEJe","requestRef":"1552146e-7569-4ada-bda2-7e6efda821f9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"604b7b61-ad3b-4498-8eae-0bab860a01f8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:05:03.813Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"604b7b61-ad3b-4498-8eae-0bab860a01f8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e57db944-5f0f-46d0-9176-157533ac4630","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017F1HTeKG3xPHL5N8yeWC8L","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c48b2d05-328d-4a59-bf3a-e9831d6b5455","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:05:04.161Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":12,"newStart":1,"newLines":15,"lines":[" # Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)"," ","-Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.","+Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 123). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py."," "," ## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06"," "," - The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser."," - The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".","-- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.","+- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000. It should look celebratory: the boards show a gradient banner, \"Double credits on everything\", and a \"2× launch bonus\" badge with the usual amount struck through on every card.","+- Account shows the plan's price as a line the server sends; no price is hardcoded in the app.","+- Delete account lives at the end of Preferences › Account, not on the server's page.","+- Usage per day and per chat lives on the server's page, now \"Billing and usage\", not in the app."," "," Everything below that is not in this list is a proposal."," "]},{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":22,"newStart":23,"newLines":23,"lines":[" - **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it."," - **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link."," - **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.","-- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.","+- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-sent price line, a bar per kind of credit, the savings-alert switch, and Delete account (the app's own confirmation dialog, whose sentence the server sends; then DELETE /v2/account and sign out). \"Get more credits\", the ring's \"See usage\" and \"Billing and usage\" open the sheet."," - **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\"."," "," Server (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:"," - **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out."," - **Chargebee checkout**, as today."," - **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.","-- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.","-- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.","+- **Billing and usage:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, credits left, and credits used per day and per chat. The server doesn't know chat titles today (`account.py` names a row by its chat id). Titles are generated through the gateway (request kind `title`), so it can keep the title it returns.","+- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line, the delete warning and the savings alert."," "," ## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)"," ","-1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".","+1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. New fields: the plan's price line and the delete warning, each a finished sentence; the price line reads a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\"."," 2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that."," 3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.","-4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.","+4. **DELETE /v2/account** deletes the account; the app then signs out.","+5. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written."," "," ## Constraints found"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"604b7b61-ad3b-4498-8eae-0bab860a01f8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
