{"parentUuid":"4ff2ffcb-536a-450d-b39e-654f1d490701","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn3BQ2NJKtxJ639P6xcu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made all four changes and published them to the canvas (version 123, the \"Credits & plans\" page). Images of the changed boards are posted above.\n\n**Launch offer.** Every pricing page now opens with a purple-to-pink banner with sparkles: \"Launch celebration · Double credits on everything\", and under it \"Every credit pack, and every month of every plan, until 31 Jan\". Each card has a pink \"2× launch bonus\" badge, with the usual amount struck through beside the doubled one: ~~500~~ 1,000 credits, ~~750~~ 1,500, ~~1,000~~ 2,000. After checkout, the confirmation carries a \"Doubled for the launch\" badge and says \"A 500-credit pack, doubled for the launch.\" The colours come from the brand tokens.\n\n**Price line.** Account's line \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\" arrives from the server as a finished sentence in the account data the app already reads. The app has no price, discount or plan wording in its code.\n\n**Delete account.** It's now the last group in Preferences › Account, with the design system's red danger button. Clicking it opens the app's own confirmation dialog. The server writes the dialog's sentence, so it can name the plan that ends and the credits that go. Confirming tells the server to delete the account, and the app then signs out. The server's page no longer has it.\n\n**Usage.** The chart and the per-chat table moved to the server's page, now titled \"Billing and usage\". It holds the plan, payment method and invoices, credits left, and usage. In the app, the button in Account and \"See usage\" in the balance panel both open that page in the sheet. Account keeps the plan, the credit bars, the alert switch and Delete account.\n\n**One gap: the server doesn't know chat titles today.** The server's account code (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`) has a comment saying the gateway never sees a chat's title, so it names each usage row by chat id. The app gets its chat titles by asking the model through the same gateway, but the server doesn't keep that title answer. The simplest fix is for the server to save the title it returns for each chat. I haven't tried it; it's work for whoever builds the Billing and usage page.\n\nThe spec is updated at [money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md](money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md). It lists what you've agreed to separately from what is still my proposal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":325772,"output_tokens":788,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":788,"cache_read_input_tokens":325772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":305},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn3BPhXSWEFb3mHtB3Vx","requestRef":"f4b64291-ce14-4912-b789-e440e67a2586","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1ac86e4-93d3-4fb9-bf7e-2fee5127a6e6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:05:19.544Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
