{"parentUuid":"05e63d83-c415-46ba-84fa-16ebf55e0a45","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5032740b-e27f-4a0d-ac75-b9a46d740f30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); first-run-flow = local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle, started by first-run-flow). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<!-- reply 1 -->\n> One gap: the server doesn’t know chat titles today. The server’s account code (web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py) has a comment saying the gateway never sees a chat’s title, so it names each usage row by chat id. The app gets its chat titles by asking the model through the same gateway, but the server doesn’t keep that title answer. The simplest fix is for the server to save the title it returns for each chat. I haven’t tried it; it’s work for whoever builds the Billing and usage page.\n\nNot sure if I completely understood what this issue is all about. But can we also pass the chat title to the server when we are recording the usage? So basically we have two columns on the server. One is chat ID, the other is chat title. I know it's not the most normalized design, but it's probably okay. Am I completely missing your point?\n\n\n\"alert me when sub will save money\" should go to the pricing page, directly in the credit pack so that the user has the full picture for all the options. If possible, we should also add a auto reload to the pricing page and or the billing page."}]},"uuid":"0184cdc1-0c34-4ef6-b5a6-430701e99dc7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:16:08.283Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":24,"turnIndex":35},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
