{"parentUuid":"f6500953-3c65-4780-b14c-6509234671d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn4Ba6DhiJv5sKWasNeH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Chat titles: you didn't miss anything, and your idea is better than mine.** Here's the issue in one case. Someone opens Billing and usage and sees a row: \"19 Nov · Expert · 40 credits\". The chat column needs a name like \"Resizing a Print to Fit the Bambu A1 mini\". The server only knows the chat's id, because titles live in the app. Your fix works: the app sends the chat's current title with each request, and the server stores it beside the chat id.\n\nIt also handles a case mine didn't. People can rename a chat in the app, and the app's chat code does have a rename action. With your approach the newest title wins, so a renamed chat shows its new name. Two small details whoever builds it should handle:\n- **The first message** goes out before the chat has a title. The row fills in with the next request.\n- **Older app versions** send no title, so their rows need a fallback such as \"Untitled chat\".\n\nI've put this on the Billing and usage board and in the spec.\n\n**What changed on the canvas** (version 125; images above):\n- **The Credit pack card** has two tick boxes above its Buy button.\n  - \"Auto-reload: buy another pack when I drop below 50 credits\": off until the person ticks it, and charged to the card used for the pack.\n  - \"Tell me if a plan would have cost me less\": on by default, and shown once above the message box. The person now sees every way to pay on one card.\n- **For a Hobby subscriber**, the same card shows auto-reload already on.\n- **Billing and usage** has a row \"Auto-reload is on\" with Change and Turn off buttons. It explains that a pack costs $10, gives 1,000 credits during the launch, and is bought whenever the balance drops below 50.\n- **Preferences › Account** no longer has the Alerts group. It shows the plan, the credit bars and Delete account.\n\nThe spec at [money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md](money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md) lists these as agreed.\n\n**Decision needed: when should auto-reload buy a pack?** I drew \"below 50 credits\" as a placeholder. The pack is the only thing auto-reload buys, $10 for 500 credits (1,000 during the launch). At 50, about 10 Expert messages are left when the purchase happens, so the person never hits the out-of-credits card mid-chat. A lower number, such as 10, charges later but risks a message that can't be paid while a card payment is still being approved. A setting the person chooses adds a control to the card. I'd keep a fixed 50."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":348164,"output_tokens":831,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":348164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn4BZocBS2uVVLPkSywj","requestRef":"273fc010-78bb-437c-ba0a-87c5379fa149","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b5c66ed-7f9d-4901-94f8-71fd0edb9a4c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:18:29.788Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b4