{"parentUuid":"a1c0f0b5-6c2a-48e7-8a9b-cd33e43b29f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn5zS1xrGbwgtzrkHX2X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10129,"cache_read_input_tokens":358281,"output_tokens":2489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1578},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2489,"cache_read_input_tokens":358281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20000,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn5zJVHKDv978nAe7RoS","requestRef":"9f8eeca0-dc89-43bf-91df-60a3e8986534","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9529ea4-3a28-4142-9da5-7b2a046a27d6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:42:24.206Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"a9529ea4-3a28-4142-9da5-7b2a046a27d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn5zS1xrGbwgtzrkHX2X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, the app can do this. There's one choice to make first: whether the server sends words or a whole page. Take the launch offer as the example. Alex opens Preferences › Account in January and sees the purple \"Double credits on everything until 31 Jan\" block above their plan, with a \"See the offer\" button that opens Credits and plans in the sheet. In February the server sends nothing and the block disappears. The space is hidden when the server sends nothing, when it's offline, or when the app is on someone's own API key. It never delays the rest of the page.\n\n**Decision needed: what does the server send for that block?**\n\n- **Words, which the app lays out.** The account data the app already loads gets one more field. It holds a small label (\"LAUNCH CELEBRATION\"), a headline, a sentence, a button label with a page name, and a style name such as \"celebrate\". The app draws it with its own design-system parts, including the gradient and sparkles from the pricing page. It shows up at the same moment as the rest of Account, because it arrives with the same data. Nothing from the server runs inside the app.\n  - Cost: the server can change the words, dates, button and destination any day, but not the layout. A new shape, such as a picture or a countdown, needs an app release, and only new app versions would show it.\n- **A small server page shown in a box.** The block is a sandboxed frame showing a page the server serves. An empty answer keeps it hidden. The server can change anything at any time, including pictures and layout. This is the closest to \"a blank div that shows whatever the server passes\".\n  - Cost: it loads after the page around it, so it pops in a moment later and has to tell the app its height.\n  - Cost: it has to be locked down. The app's web pages carry a channel that can call into the native app. I haven't checked whether that channel also reaches a frame inside the page. Ruling that out is a must before building.\n  - Cost: the server has to copy the app's colours and fonts itself to look like the rest of Account.\n- **A piece of HTML dropped straight into the div.** It looks quick, but I'd avoid it. The app would have to strip anything that could run. The HTML would also style itself with the app's CSS class names, so those names quietly become part of the contract. Rename a class and old banners break.\n\nI recommend words that the app lays out, at least for the launch. The launch block is words and a button, and this way it can't break, can't flicker and can't reach into the app. If you expect promotions with pictures or unusual layouts later, the server page is the better long-term choice, once the native-channel question is checked.\n\nBoth options fit the contract we already drew. The block is one more server-written item, next to the plan's price line and the delete warning. Its button opens a page through the same page-link request the sheet uses.\n\nWhich do you want the server to send: words, or a page? Tell me and I'll draw the block on the Account boards."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10129,"cache_read_input_tokens":358281,"output_tokens":2489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1578},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10129,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2489,"cache_read_input_tokens":358281,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10129,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10129},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgn5zJVHKDv978nAe7RoS","requestRef":"9f8eeca0-dc89-43bf-91df-60a3e8986534","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"514485b3-5b1f-450f-bbe4-01068adab13c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:42:35.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
